{
 "OpenDroid is an autonomous AI assistant that runs entirely on your Android device. ": 1,
 "We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring transparency about how your data is handled. ": 1,
 "This policy explains what data OpenDroid collects, how it is used, and your rights regarding that data.": 1,
 "OpenDroid processes the following data locally on your device:\\n\\n": 1,
 "• Voice commands and text queries you provide\\n": 1,
 "• Device state information (battery level, WiFi status, connectivity)\\n": 1,
 "• Contact names for resolving communication actions\\n": 1,
 "• Conversation history for context-aware responses\\n": 1,
 "• User preferences and semantic memory facts you share\\n\\n": 1,
 "All data is stored in a local Room database on your device. No data is collected by the OpenDroid developers.": 1,
 "OpenDroid sends your queries to the LLM provider you configure (e.g., Google Gemini, OpenAI, Anthropic, Groq, etc.) ": 1,
 "to generate responses and action plans. Each provider has its own privacy policy governing how they handle your data.\\n\\n": 1,
 "• Your API keys are stored locally on your device and are never transmitted to OpenDroid servers.\\n": 1,
 "• Query data sent to LLM providers is subject to their respective privacy policies.\\n": 1,
 "• You can switch providers or use local models (Ollama) at any time to keep data fully on-device.": 1,
 "OpenDroid requests the following permissions to function:\\n\\n": 1,
 "• Microphone — For voice command input\\n": 1,
 "• Accessibility Service — For automating app interactions (WhatsApp, etc.)\\n": 1,
 "• Contacts — For resolving contact names to phone numbers\\n": 1,
 "• Phone — For placing calls\\n": 1,
 "• SMS — For sending text messages\\n": 1,
 "• Camera — For taking photos/flashlight control\\n": 1,
 "• Storage — For file management actions\\n": 1,
 "• Location — For weather and directions features\\n\\n": 1,
 "All permissions are optional. Features requiring ungranted permissions will gracefully degrade or prompt you.": 1,
 "OpenDroid uses Android Accessibility Service to automate app interactions ": 1,
 "(such as sending WhatsApp messages) when you explicitly request it.\\n\\n": 1,
 "The Accessibility Service:\\n\\n": 1,
 "• Only activates when you enable it in Android Settings\\n": 1,
 "• Only acts when you give OpenDroid a command\\n": 1,
 "• Does NOT run in the background without your command\\n": 1,
 "• Does NOT read passwords or banking information\\n": 1,
 "• Does NOT record or log screen content passively\\n": 1,
 "• Does NOT collect, store, or transmit any data observed through the Accessibility Service to external servers\\n\\n": 1,
 "The service is used solely to perform on-screen actions you request, such as tapping buttons or typing text in other apps. ": 1,
 "You can revoke Accessibility Service access at any time from Android Settings > Accessibility > OpenDroid.": 1,
 "• All conversation history, memory facts, and task logs are stored in a local SQLite database on your device.\\n": 1,
 "• Memory entries support time-to-live (TTL) and are automatically cleaned on expiration.\\n": 1,
 "• Execution history remains until you clear it from System Logs or uninstall the app.\\n": 1,
 "• Saving a completed task as a macro is an explicit user action; API keys, tokens, passwords, and recognized credentials are replaced with [REDACTED] before recording.\\n": 1,
 "• You can clear any memory type (Working, Episodic, Semantic, Procedural) from the Memory screen.\\n": 1,
 "• Uninstalling the app removes all stored data permanently.": 1,
 "OpenDroid does NOT:\\n\\n": 1,
 "• Sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties\\n": 1,
 "• Collect analytics, telemetry, or usage statistics\\n": 1,
 "• Transmit data to any server owned by the OpenDroid team\\n": 1,
 "• Display advertisements or use ad-tracking technologies\\n\\n": 1,
 "The only external data transmission occurs when your queries are sent to the LLM provider you have configured.": 1,
 "• API keys are stored with Android Keystore AES-256-GCM encryption on your device.\\n": 1,
 "• Your profile name and birth date are encrypted the same way, with a separate device key.\\n": 1,
 "• Encryption keys never leave the device's hardware-backed keystore, so encrypted values cannot be read on another device or restored from a backup.\\n": 1,
 "• If a key is invalidated, the affected values are not recoverable and are never rewritten unencrypted; the app asks you to enter them again.\\n": 1,
 "• Ordinary non-personal settings, such as whether onboarding is complete, are stored unencrypted in app-private storage.\\n": 1,
 "• All LLM API communication uses HTTPS encryption.\\n": 1,
 "• The accessibility service only activates when explicitly enabled by you.\\n": 1,
 "• Destructive actions (device restart, file deletion) require user confirmation.": 1,
 "OpenDroid is not intended for use by children under 13 years of age. ": 1,
 "We do not knowingly collect information from children.": 1,
 "We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected in the app with an updated \\\"Last updated\\\" date. ": 1,
 "Continued use of OpenDroid after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.": 1,
 "If you have questions about this privacy policy or OpenDroid's data practices, ": 1,
 "please open an issue on our GitHub repository (yashab-cyber/opendroid) or contact the development team.\\n\\n": 1,
